{"name":"Tezcatlipōca Blue","hex":"#5500ee","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tezcatlipoca","blocks":[{"text":"Tezcatlipoca was a central deity in Aztec religion. He is associated with a variety of concepts, including the night sky, hurricanes, obsidian, and conflict. He was considered one of the four sons of Ometecuhtli and Omecihuatl, the primordial dual deity. His main festival was Toxcatl, which, like most religious festivals of Aztec culture, involved human sacrifice."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tezcatlipoca.png/330px-Tezcatlipoca.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tezcatlipoca","wikidata":"Q756797"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Standing_jaguar.jpg/500px-Standing_jaguar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Standing_jaguar.jpg/500px-Standing_jaguar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The jaguar was an animal sacred to Tezcatlipoca.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStanding_jaguar.jpg%23%2Fmedia"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg/500px-John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg/1280px-John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg/500px-John_Dee%27s_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aztec obsidian mirror","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohn_Dee's_mirror_British_Museum_26_07_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg/500px-Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg/1280px-Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg/500px-Black_Tezcatlipoca.jpg?utm